WEBVTT

00:00:00.640 --> 00:00:03.650
I'm gonna be the first-star idol one day!

00:00:03.650 --> 00:00:07.730
Nijino Yume's about to start her Aikatsu!{upon retrospect this might be better as "Nijino Yume's about"}

00:00:09.190 --> 00:00:12.150
The foundation of singing lies in voice projection.

00:00:12.530 --> 00:00:16.280
Everyone try to hold this note as long as you can.

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:17.530
Ready...

00:00:17.530 --> 00:00:19.240
Start!

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:37.260
Okay, good job.

00:00:39.260 --> 00:00:41.390
I'm still hearing some discord. {I thought this was spelled dischord}{why would you think that}

00:00:41.390 --> 00:00:44.310
Seems we'll need to stretch those bodies first.

00:00:44.310 --> 00:00:46.190
Let's start!

00:00:47.610 --> 00:00:49.150
You really are awesome, Rola.

00:00:49.610 --> 00:00:52.280
It sounded like you could've kept on going.

00:00:52.740 --> 00:00:55.660
It's because I've been taking lessons since I was a kid. {for a long time now}

00:00:55.990 --> 00:00:57.950
For that long?

00:00:57.950 --> 00:01:01.330
What about you, Yume? 
Ever learn anything useful?

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:05.830
I was in the volleyball club during elementary school.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.290
We would run day after day,

00:01:09.290 --> 00:01:11.420
and shout a whole bunch too.

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:14.920
I was the loudest one there.

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:19.390
So my stamina and loudness are top-notch. {I'm pretty damn certain this is right}

00:01:20.260 --> 00:01:22.970
Projecting your voice is different from just being loud.

00:01:22.970 --> 00:01:24.930
I figured...

00:01:29.230 --> 00:01:32.400
<i>Am I already too far behind?</i>

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:33.780
Fix your posture.

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:37.910
Feet shoulder-width apart. Open up your chest.

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:41.280
Pull in your chin, and relax your throat and shoulders.

00:01:41.700 --> 00:01:43.700
Sing from your stomach.

00:01:43.700 --> 00:01:45.790
Let's give it one more try!

00:01:45.790 --> 00:01:46.580
Okay!

00:01:56.720 --> 00:02:00.180
It was much easier that time, 
and it worked much better too!

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:02.600
<i>That's</i> projection.

00:02:05.060 --> 00:02:07.190
Okay, babies.

00:02:07.190 --> 00:02:10.940
The class sorting auditions are almost here.

00:02:11.310 --> 00:02:14.530
The Flower Song Class, Bird Theater Class,

00:02:14.530 --> 00:02:17.570
Wind Dance Class, and Moon Beauty Class.

00:02:17.570 --> 00:02:22.160
Choosing which class to enter is another part of self-producing.

00:02:22.160 --> 00:02:25.660
Everyone, pick one to aim for!

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:26.830
Get on it! {for now}

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:09.100
Aozora Hiyoko! A fledgling like you is no more than a burden! {yes, this is her name}

00:04:09.100 --> 00:04:10.220
Go home!

00:04:10.600 --> 00:04:12.730
No, I will not!

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:16.360
I may be a clumsy and clueless fledgling now...

00:04:16.730 --> 00:04:20.740
But one day... I want to spread my wings in the great blue sky!

00:04:21.400 --> 00:04:25.110
I swear... I'll become a flight attendant! {this was obvious to me, I assume it is to everyone else that it's cabin attendant}{this is nowhere near obvious, nor is CA/cabin attendant common english usage}

00:04:28.240 --> 00:04:33.370
You can do it! Hiyoko-chan, 
you can become a flight attendant!

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:36.250
Was that scene really so emotional?

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:41.590
It's just... I could feel Hiyoko-chan's emotions like they were my own.

00:04:43.170 --> 00:04:45.260
Yume-chan, you really love it, don't you?

00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:49.010
The morning drama, "Rise of a Flight Attendant".

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:52.850
Tsubasa-senpai's acting is something else.

00:04:52.850 --> 00:04:54.100
Yeah, yeah!

00:04:55.810 --> 00:04:56.770
Who were you again?

00:04:57.100 --> 00:04:59.980
It's the first time we've met. I'm Nanakura Koharu.

00:04:59.980 --> 00:05:01.650
Yume-chan and I are childhood friends.

00:05:02.650 --> 00:05:03.780
I see.

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:08.660
I'm Yume's classmate, 
Sakuraba Rola. Nice to meet you.

00:05:08.660 --> 00:05:10.530
Nice to meet you too, Rola-san.

00:05:10.530 --> 00:05:14.750
Just drop the honorifics. 
Let's have lunch together, Koharu.

00:05:16.790 --> 00:05:18.830
I'd love to, Rola!

00:05:20.800 --> 00:05:23.170
Which are you aiming for in the class sorting audition?

00:05:24.220 --> 00:05:26.380
I'm going for the Beauty Class.

00:05:26.380 --> 00:05:27.430
So you are.

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:29.140
What about you?

00:05:29.140 --> 00:05:30.640
I'm set on the Song Class.

00:05:30.640 --> 00:05:32.890
Same as Yume-chan, then.

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:37.560
Yume-chan?

00:05:38.150 --> 00:05:40.110
You're auditioning for Song Class, right?

00:05:42.070 --> 00:05:44.320
That's the plan, yes...

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:49.370
But there are so many other girls who are much better at singing than me.

00:05:50.370 --> 00:05:55.080
Plus, you know how low the acceptance rate is for the Song Class too. {I don't know why the language to describe this is opposite of english}{I don't think japanese does this with other ritsus, does it?}

00:05:55.500 --> 00:05:57.830
You can make it, Yume-chan.

00:05:58.790 --> 00:06:03.090
You were able to pull off a performance so amazing it surprised everyone.

00:06:03.800 --> 00:06:07.760
But... I don't remember doing that.

00:06:07.760 --> 00:06:10.090
A performance like that is no fluke.

00:06:12.310 --> 00:06:12.970
Here.

00:06:13.390 --> 00:06:15.680
Eat up and get some energy.

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:18.190
You're supposed to be my rival.

00:06:18.190 --> 00:06:20.100
Thanks, Rola!

00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:35.950
Everyone's training on their own.

00:06:35.950 --> 00:06:38.160
Okay, then I will too!

00:06:50.340 --> 00:06:54.010
H-Huh? My voice isn't coming out right.

00:06:55.010 --> 00:06:56.270
<i>At this rate...</i>

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:01.020
You fail.

00:07:01.770 --> 00:07:03.150
Please wait!

00:07:03.150 --> 00:07:06.150
I know I have enough stamina for this!

00:07:06.440 --> 00:07:10.070
There's more to being an idol than just stamina.

00:07:11.360 --> 00:07:13.030
Bye-bee!

00:07:16.160 --> 00:07:18.040
No!

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:20.290
Stop, stop, stop!

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:24.420
I need to train! I have to figure out a way to train!

00:07:32.510 --> 00:07:34.220
It looks deserted.

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:37.390
Okay, this place should be fine.

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:57.830
<i>Rola could go on for much longer.</i>

00:07:58.990 --> 00:08:00.370
<i>If I don't do something...</i>

00:08:03.000 --> 00:08:05.380
Enough negativity!

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:09.880
Don't give in, Yume! No more negativity! {it's a joudan}

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:16.180
Tsubasa-senpai!

00:08:17.510 --> 00:08:20.020
Oh, sorry for giggling.

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:22.140
Don't be!

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:27.190
There's no need to be on edge. 
We're both students of the same school.

00:08:27.190 --> 00:08:28.520
O-Okay then.

00:08:30.030 --> 00:08:31.900
That thing you're holding...

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:34.910
Isn't that a script for "Rise of a Flight Attendant"?{sorry, you're going to have to change the typesetting}

00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:36.870
Oh, yes.

00:08:37.950 --> 00:08:41.700
I've watched every single episode of 
"Rise of a Flight Attendant"!

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:47.710
Seeing Hiyoko-chan work so hard inspires me to do my best too!

00:08:48.460 --> 00:08:49.920
Thank you.

00:08:51.260 --> 00:08:54.430
Um, were you just about to practice your lines?

00:08:54.840 --> 00:08:59.350
Well, I did plan on memorizing the script out here.

00:08:59.350 --> 00:09:02.930
I-I'm sorry for disturbing you!

00:09:03.310 --> 00:09:04.640
I'll excuse myself!

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:11.480
Um...

00:09:11.480 --> 00:09:12.440
What is it?

00:09:13.190 --> 00:09:15.820
Tsubasa-senpai, were you worried at all?

00:09:16.320 --> 00:09:18.450
When you had your class sorting audition.

00:09:18.910 --> 00:09:21.910
S-Sorry for asking something so strange.

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:26.830
I'm sure you went straight for the Theater Class.

00:09:26.830 --> 00:09:27.710
I didn't.

00:09:27.710 --> 00:09:28.710
Huh?

00:09:29.840 --> 00:09:33.090
I was in the Song Class at first.

00:09:47.060 --> 00:09:50.980
That's right. I was in the Song Class at first.

00:09:50.980 --> 00:09:52.570
Really?

00:09:53.030 --> 00:09:56.070
To be the brightest star of Four Star Academy.

00:09:56.070 --> 00:10:00.950
To be at the top of the Song Class—that was my dream.{we should have a character talk like a pirate despite having no reason to do so}

00:10:02.280 --> 00:10:07.830
I passed the Song Class audition, 
and everything seemed to be going my way.

00:10:12.460 --> 00:10:15.970
That was, until...

00:10:16.420 --> 00:10:17.590
I met Hime.

00:10:20.180 --> 00:10:22.600
I was confident I wouldn't lose to anyone...

00:10:23.430 --> 00:10:25.680
right up until I saw her perform.

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:35.690
I could feel it in my bones that she would be the best in Song Class.

00:10:37.190 --> 00:10:40.570
I went to mull over what I should do next,

00:10:41.780 --> 00:10:44.990
and it was then that Yachigusa Momoko-sensei from the Theater Class appeared.

00:10:47.120 --> 00:10:49.120
What a nice breeze.

00:10:50.920 --> 00:10:54.630
It makes me want to just fly off somewhere.

00:10:57.760 --> 00:10:59.300
Th-That's dangerous!

00:11:02.010 --> 00:11:03.640
Just kidding.

00:11:05.810 --> 00:11:07.890
Please don't joke around about that.

00:11:07.890 --> 00:11:10.270
I just wanted to clear the air.

00:11:10.270 --> 00:11:15.650
You looked like you were convinced the sky was falling.

00:11:17.530 --> 00:11:21.320
"There's no point if I can't be the top idol of Song Class."

00:11:21.990 --> 00:11:23.530
Did I get it right?

00:11:26.830 --> 00:11:29.040
You're thinking too small.

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:34.290
You have such wonderful wings, yet you're not using them to fly.

00:11:34.790 --> 00:11:36.000
Fly?

00:11:36.000 --> 00:11:39.550
Say, why do you think birds fly?

00:11:40.550 --> 00:11:42.800
Because... they have wings.

00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:45.510
Because they have the will to fly.

00:11:46.430 --> 00:11:50.890
The thing about being an actress isn't that you compete with others.

00:11:50.890 --> 00:11:53.020
You face and fight yourself.

00:11:53.810 --> 00:11:58.570
Since there are no right answers in acting, you'll never run out of worries.

00:11:59.360 --> 00:12:02.450
Even so, never giving up the chase for your own answer

00:12:02.450 --> 00:12:05.700
is how we spread our wings and fly.

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:09.830
That is the way of the Bird Theater Class.

00:12:11.960 --> 00:12:17.670
What a nice breeze. It's the perfect day to set flight for a new world.

00:12:19.130 --> 00:12:21.470
In order to face and fight myself,

00:12:22.260 --> 00:12:25.470
I decided to transfer into the Theater Class.

00:12:26.680 --> 00:12:30.970
I may be at the top of Theater Class, but I'm not done with my flight.

00:12:30.970 --> 00:12:34.690
The world is vast, and countless roads await.

00:12:35.270 --> 00:12:37.980
Waver, worry, struggle,

00:12:38.270 --> 00:12:40.480
and you may one day reach your dream.

00:12:41.240 --> 00:12:41.990
Bye.

00:12:47.570 --> 00:12:49.280
Thank you very much.

00:12:58.130 --> 00:13:01.510
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:13:01.880 --> 00:13:07.140
<i>I thought I wanted to be like Hime-senpai after seeing her sing on stage.</i>

00:13:26.910 --> 00:13:28.820
Heck yeah!

00:13:35.830 --> 00:13:37.790
Hey, you all right?

00:13:39.960 --> 00:13:41.300
I won!

00:13:46.430 --> 00:13:47.800
What now?!

00:13:50.550 --> 00:13:53.810
You're bright red. I knew you were a boiled octopus. {I think I forgot to mention this change on the blog, better do it this time}

00:13:53.810 --> 00:13:56.640
Come on, stop it with that already!

00:13:57.850 --> 00:14:01.190
I'm impressed you managed to keep pace with me.

00:14:01.190 --> 00:14:04.940
Not like being good at sprinting is actually going to help me pass.

00:14:06.530 --> 00:14:08.700
My class sorting audition.

00:14:08.700 --> 00:14:10.070
Oh.

00:14:10.070 --> 00:14:13.370
If I can't pass...

00:14:13.370 --> 00:14:15.450
You just want to pass?

00:14:17.250 --> 00:14:22.960
Isn't the important thing not about whether you can pass, but what you want to accomplish?

00:14:25.010 --> 00:14:28.840
Didn't you come to Four Star Academy with a goal in mind?

00:14:29.380 --> 00:14:33.890
Sprint straight towards it, like you did just now.

00:14:34.520 --> 00:14:35.850
Later.

00:14:39.350 --> 00:14:41.440
A goal...

00:14:43.190 --> 00:14:44.610
That's right!

00:14:51.110 --> 00:14:54.120
We will now hold the auditions for Song Class.

00:14:54.490 --> 00:14:55.490
Okay.

00:14:55.490 --> 00:14:58.080
I'll begin by explaining the audition's structure.

00:14:58.080 --> 00:14:59.870
I'm sorry I'm late!

00:15:01.920 --> 00:15:05.880
I didn't realize how much time had passed when I was choosing my dress.

00:15:07.840 --> 00:15:11.340
Nijino Yume, here for the Song Class audition!

00:15:12.640 --> 00:15:15.390
It's that time of the year again!

00:15:15.720 --> 00:15:20.270
Four Star Academy's Spring Festival, the class sorting auditions!

00:15:22.310 --> 00:15:28.650
Participants' scores will be a combined result of the votes from each class's teachers, S4, and the audience.

00:15:28.650 --> 00:15:33.030
Let's start the Spring Festival!

00:15:43.040 --> 00:15:44.920
<i>I love to sing.</i>

00:15:44.920 --> 00:15:47.960
<i>Even if I'm not as good as the other girls,</i>

00:15:49.630 --> 00:15:50.760
<i>I want to sing.</i>

00:15:51.430 --> 00:15:53.930
<i>My passion for singing is stronger than everyone else's!</i>

00:15:54.800 --> 00:15:59.310
<i>I'll use this Pink Coord, full of hearts and passion.</i>

00:19:17.550 --> 00:19:22.390
She didn't quite live up to the standards of her debut performance.

00:19:22.390 --> 00:19:25.600
But you could really hear the fun in her voice!

00:19:27.390 --> 00:19:28.600
You certainly could.

00:19:28.600 --> 00:19:33.440
Your strong desire to sing came through loud and clear.

00:19:39.070 --> 00:19:41.450
This concludes the auditions.

00:19:41.910 --> 00:19:43.950
It's time to announce the results.

00:19:44.530 --> 00:19:46.450
S4, take it away.

00:19:47.990 --> 00:19:51.960
First, the Beauty Class results.

00:19:52.790 --> 00:19:56.090
Oda Masumi. Iwasaki Mika.

00:19:56.090 --> 00:19:58.050
Nanakura Koharu.

00:20:00.300 --> 00:20:02.930
You did it! You made it, Koharu-chan!

00:20:02.930 --> 00:20:04.430
You passed!

00:20:04.430 --> 00:20:06.600
Yeah, thanks!

00:20:08.060 --> 00:20:10.600
Now announcing the results for Song Class.

00:20:11.140 --> 00:20:11.980
In first place is...

00:20:12.600 --> 00:20:14.600
Sakuraba Rola.

00:20:15.060 --> 00:20:18.020
Well done, Rola! You're at the top.

00:20:18.020 --> 00:20:19.150
Of course.

00:20:20.900 --> 00:20:23.860
And lastly, the final acceptant is...

00:20:25.700 --> 00:20:27.030
Nijino Yume.

00:20:30.080 --> 00:20:33.290
D-Did she just say Nijino Yume?

00:20:33.290 --> 00:20:34.620
She said it!

00:20:34.620 --> 00:20:36.500
Congrats, Yume!

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:37.790
Y-Yeah.

00:20:40.090 --> 00:20:40.920
I...

00:20:41.550 --> 00:20:44.220
I did it!

00:20:46.510 --> 00:20:48.760
Yume-chan, I'm so happy for you.

00:20:48.760 --> 00:20:49.640
Thanks!

00:20:50.720 --> 00:20:51.680
Huh?

00:20:52.850 --> 00:20:53.940
What's this?

00:20:54.980 --> 00:20:58.650
I got the same thing. I wonder what it is.

00:20:58.650 --> 00:21:00.190
It's Glitter. {caps?}{one cap, but not all caps (also, I wonder what the world would be like if we chose to make kirakiratter "glitter")}

00:21:00.190 --> 00:21:01.650
Glitter?

00:21:01.650 --> 00:21:02.570
Yo.

00:21:04.070 --> 00:21:05.820
Looks like you scraped by.

00:21:06.360 --> 00:21:07.570
Boiled octo.

00:21:08.160 --> 00:21:12.200
Gosh, I thought I told you to stop with that already!

00:21:12.200 --> 00:21:13.830
Huh?! No way!

00:21:14.210 --> 00:21:15.710
It's really them!

00:21:15.710 --> 00:21:18.000
Huh, you know him?

00:21:18.000 --> 00:21:18.880
Huh?

00:21:18.880 --> 00:21:21.590
Yume, don't tell me you had no idea.

00:21:21.590 --> 00:21:24.420
He's Yuuki Subaru-kun, from M4! {you know, it's a splice, but I think it's okay}

00:21:25.630 --> 00:21:27.220
M4?

00:21:28.050 --> 00:21:31.060
Any magazine with their name on it sells out instantly!

00:21:31.060 --> 00:21:35.100
Ratings go through the roof whenever they appear on TV!

00:21:35.640 --> 00:21:39.310
Tickets for all their concerts sell out in five minutes!

00:21:39.310 --> 00:21:44.030
M4 is the top group of Four Star Academy's boys division!

00:21:46.660 --> 00:21:48.910
So you were an idol too.

00:21:50.120 --> 00:21:52.540
You seriously didn't know me?

00:21:52.990 --> 00:21:55.660
I couldn't care less about M4!

00:21:55.660 --> 00:21:58.790
S4's the only group I love.

00:21:59.130 --> 00:22:03.000
This girl... she's really got some nerve.

00:22:03.000 --> 00:22:06.420
Sounds like we still have a ways to go, Subaru-kun.

00:22:06.420 --> 00:22:09.680
Come on, our class activities start tomorrow.

00:22:09.680 --> 00:22:10.640
Let's go!

00:22:11.180 --> 00:22:12.140
Sure...

00:22:12.970 --> 00:22:14.180
Wait up!

00:22:14.640 --> 00:22:16.100
Yume-chan!

00:22:16.100 --> 00:22:18.270
Why are you running?

00:22:18.900 --> 00:22:22.900
I don't even know myself!

00:23:58.620 --> 00:24:02.120
We held the Spring Festival, also known as the class sorting auditions.

00:24:02.120 --> 00:24:04.500
Bust down the gates of your own future!

00:24:04.500 --> 00:24:06.750
That's the spirit of self-production!

00:24:06.750 --> 00:24:09.510
We've all got high expectations for your growth!

00:24:11.220 --> 00:24:13.970
We're going to appear on Aikatsu TV?

00:24:13.970 --> 00:24:15.600
Wait, this isn't right!

00:24:15.600 --> 00:24:17.970
Just eat this bagel sandwich for now.

00:24:18.520 --> 00:24:20.430
Next time on Aikatsu Stars!

00:24:20.430 --> 00:24:22.190
Always at One Hundred Percent!

00:24:22.190 --> 00:24:24.600
Become the first-star idol!
